projects.description:
A for policy development,  capacity building of national level, and evidence based advocacy to promote equitable access to pre-school education and quality early learning opportunities;
Capacitating preschools for implementation of new PSE Curriculum Framework through trainings, mentoring, horizontal exchange and monitoring;
Supporting further development of an inclusive online learning system and strengthening capacity of institutions for its delivery, management and monitoring, modernization of teaching practice and development of new support mechanisms to schools and teachers;  Promotion and advocacy for inclusive education
Establishing education technology libraries in schools, developing capacities of teachers for online and hybrid learning, provision of technical support aimed at strengthening institutional capacities for policy development, financing, management, coordination and monitoring of quality inclusive education, Strenghtening capacities of education and other professionals to  implement inclusive pedagogy and provide quality additional support, especially to children with disabilities, supporting the education of refugee and migrants’ children in Serbia.

Increased participation of young men and women in community proceses in line with international standards and Agenda 2030 by ensuring that sex-disaggregated and age-disaggregated evidence are gathered, data-base on youth participation standard developed, capacity building of  youth workers for the newly addopted NYS implementation completed.
Increased  participation through UNICEF U-Report platform with more voices of adolescent girls and boys comming from rural areas having their voices heard. 
mechanisms to improve the quality, accessibility and relevance of volunteering programmes are strengthened.
TA to Ministries and bodies at the national and local levels provided to support changes in the area of practical policies and regulatory frameworks, ensuring participation of Youth Advisory bodies and young people in consultation processes and advocacy for strategic priorities and public policies related to the overall wellbeing of children and adolescents, on local and national level, including climate change; 
- Technical support provided to the Ministry of  Tourism and Youth on the Law on Youth;
- Professional, technical and organizational support provided for the needs of the Working Group of the Ministry of Labor, Employment, Veterans and Social Affairs on Amendments to the Law on Volunteering and Internship

Support to active and effective participation by States Parties in the Implementation Review Mechanism of UNCAC;
Supporting the capacity of anti-corruption practitioners and other stakeholders to prevent and combat corruption in whole of society;
Support in mainstreaming anti-corruption into national development strategies and enhancing technical assistance programmes

The project will specifically focus on:
• enhancing the commitment and capacities of media and journalists to abide by professional and ethical standards of journalism and enhancing media accountability; 
• reinforcing freedom of expression and circulation of accurate information by an increasing rights-based regulation of digital platforms and online media;
• empowering media outlets to better cover climate change and environmental issues, through investigative journalism.
